TEXT 8 -360 Left 2 ;Result data for instance U1 = synchronous generator\n==========================================\nv(u1:usx)=ud=8.9kV/sqrt(2)=6.33kV d-axis stator voltage\nv(u1:uxy)=uq=13.6kV/sqrt(2)=9.65kV q-axis stator voltage\nv(u1:isx)=id=-19.4kA/sqrt(2)=-13.77kA d-axis stator current\nv(u1:isy)=iq=-6.72kA/sqrt(2)=-4.75kA d-axis stator current\nv(u1:imx,u1:idx)=ie'=30.2k/sqrt(2)=21.41kA magnetic field current (windings related to stator-parameter g)\nv(u1:idx,u1:isx)=0 d-axis damping current\nv(u1:imy,u1:isy)=0 q-axis damping current\nv(u1:imxa)=imuex=10.8kV/sqrt(2)=7.63kA d-axis magnetizing current\nv(u1:imya)=imuey=-6.72kV/sqrt(2)=-4.75kA q-axis magnetizing current\nxs=xd=1.225ohm\n \nFurther is valid:\nimuex=isx+idx+ie'\nimuey=isy+idy \nimue=sqrt(imuex*imuex+imuey*imuey) \nis=sqrt(isx*isx+isy*isy)\nus=sqrt(usx*usx+usy*usy)\np=3*((usx*isx)/2+(usy*isy)/2)\nq=3*((usy*isx)/2-(usx*isy)/2)\ntheta=atan2(usx,usy)\n \nStarting from diagramm 1 (voltages) : (Generator reference arrow system)\nConverting V's->VA's is by multiplication with factor : 3*Us/jXs\nThe Voltage diagram 1 is converted to the generator diagramm 3\nThe generator has UN_verkettet=20kV, f=50Hz, S=500MVA, cosphi=0.8 lagging\nThe synchronous reactance is 1.225ohm (Xd=UN/sqrt(3)/IK0 = UN/sqrt(3)/IN/KC=1.225ohm (unsaturated))\nUs=UN_verkettet/sqrt(3)=11,5kV\nIs,max=S/3/Us=500e6/3/10.5e3=14.5kA\nFor the following computation see wxmaxima file: Generatordiagramm_400kV_2.wxmx\nUs=11550\nPoint a of the diagramm:\nUs converts to line a-b: 3*Us*Us/j*Xs=-326MVar\nUp of diagramm1 is:\nUp=Us+j*Xs*I=11550+j*1.224*(14500 with angle of -36.87)\nAnd now converted to diagramm 3 length is:\nDE(a-c): 3*Us*abs(Up)/Xs=745MVA\nNow you can make a circle from a-c (Rotor currents) and b-c (Stator currents)\nUnder b the reactive power is negative\nOver b the reactive power is positive\nAt b there is the nominal UE of 600V\nAt c there is the maximal UE of 1350V\nNow we can also set the minimal UE of 200V\nFor stability reason the minimal load angle is fixed to 70 degrees\nExample: If you want to go from point c to point d:\nYou can see that the UE is not changed (a-c = a-d)\nThe generator will produce less active power and \nThe inductive reactive power output of the generator will be higher\nIf you want to hold the reactive power output constant you have to \nchange UE also to a lower value\n \nSee also diagram1.png and diagram3.png\nDiagram2.png is diagram1.png for load reference arrow system\n(as the results in ltspice which are always in LRAS)
